git-hop is a context-aware porcelain tool for managing
Git worktrees, Docker environments, and structured workspaces.

Given an argument instead of a command, git hop clones, switches or
attaches a fork:

  git hop <uri> [<path>]
      Clone mode. Clones <uri> into a new hub at <path> (default:
      <repo> in the current directory): a bare repository with the
      default branch checked out at hops/<default-branch>. An org/repo
      shorthand expands to git@<host>:org/repo.git, <host> from
      --git-domain or hop.gitDomain (default github.com).

  git hop <branch>
      Switch mode. Inside a hub, switches to the existing worktree of
      <branch>: points the hub's current symlink at it and runs the
      worktree-switch hooks. Creates nothing; 'git hop add <branch>'
      creates a worktree.

  git hop <uri> --branch <branch>
      Fork-attach mode. Inside a hub, fetches <branch> from the fork at
      <uri> and, when it shares history with the hub, checks it out as
      the worktree <branch>-fork-<owner>.

Usage:
  git-hop [flags]
  git-hop [command]

MANAGEMENT

Additional Commands:
  add            Add a new worktree and environment
  doctor         Check and repair the environment
  env            Manage the environment lifecycle
  help           Show help for a command or command group
  init           Initialize git-hop repository structure
  list           List all managed worktrees
  merge          Merge a worktree branch into a receiving branch, then delete the source worktree
  move           Rename a worktree and its branch
  prune          Remove orphaned worktrees and hubs from state and hop.json
  remove         Remove a hub, hopspace, or branch
  repair         Safely repair stale worktree metadata
  status         Show the working tree status

Flags:
      --branch string       branch name for fork-attach mode
  -n, --dry-run             preview changes without applying
      --env-start           start the new worktree's environment (default: hop.env.autoStart)
      --force               bypass safety checks
      --format string       Output format (csv, human, json, table, text, yaml) (default "table")
      --git-domain string   Git domain for shorthand notation (e.g., github.com, gitlab.com)
  -g, --global              use global hopspace in $GIT_HOP_DATA_HOME (default: local)
  -h, --help                help for git-hop
      --help-all            Show all commands including management
      --help-management     Show only management commands
      --hooks string        mirror committed .git-hop/hooks/ on clone: symlink|copy|prompt|none (default: prompt)
      --hooks-overwrite     overwrite an existing hopspace hook with different content (symlink/copy modes)
      --json                output in JSON format
      --no-color            Disable ANSI color
      --no-env-start        do not start the new worktree's environment
      --no-hints            Suppress next-step hints after command output
      --offline             Disable network access. Highest-precedence override: flips off per-command network opt-ins (peer discovery, sync, GitHub, push). Enforced beneath net/http and any client routed through netpolicy.GuardDial; loopback and diagnostics stay exempt.
      --porcelain           machine-readable output
  -q, --quiet               Suppress non-essential output
  -V, --verbose count       Increase log verbosity (-V=debug, -VV=trace)
  -v, --version             version for git-hop

Use "git-hop [command] --help" for more information about a command.
